      {
        "id": 2407119125,
        "content": "I think it could be interesting to add the query param to prefill the search filter and to ensure the page acts as expected. Basically, right now, if you toggle between the proposals and tasks view, it will show everything and not consider the value inside of the text filter box so that would also need to be fixed. \r\n`https://devpool.directory/?q=ubiquity-os-marketplace` is an example of how this can look. Perhaps the search filter box should automatically change the search query in the url bar on every key stroke so that the user can conveniently search for what they want, and then copy/paste the URL straight from their browser UI when they see the filtered views they want.\r\nIn addition, perhaps within the render function we can always check the current search query state so that it filters every time the render function is called. This should automatically solve for when we toggle between the proposals and tasks view.",
        "url": "https://github.com/ubiquity/work.ubq.fi/issues/122#issuecomment-2407119125",
        "commentType": "ISSUE_COLLABORATOR",
